# SM-T715 (armv7h) package of omarchy-mobile's omamobile-shell at commit
# 5f7ba48, trimmed to the touch shell of an 8" tablet (touch layer P2,
# docs/journal/PLAN.md §3; docs/image/ROOTFS.md "Touch layer P2").
#
# What it is: ordinary Omarchy shell plugins (QML) that turn Omarchy's shell
# into a touch shell: a status bar with a pull-down quick-settings sheet
# (omamobile.bar replaces omarchy.bar), the dock, app drawer and home pill
# (omamobile.launcher), recent apps (omamobile.switcher), home screens
# (omamobile.home; OWL widgets stay behind upstream's off-by-default flag),
# the keyboard's hide button (omamobile.keyboard) and the edge back swipe
# (omamobile.back); omamobile-setup-user links them into the user's config.
# Nothing here is compiled and nothing patches Hyprland.
#
# Kept as upstream ships them: the seven plugins above, bin/omamobile-setup-user,
# -launch, -osk-watch (keyboard visibility for the launcher and the hide
# button), -bt-agent (quick settings' Bluetooth panel), -screenrecord and
# -widget, branding/, the widget guides and examples, the polkit admin rule,
# omamobile-setup-user.service (the image masks it: docs/image/ROOTFS.md).
# Changed for the tablet:
#   - profile/shell.json is tablet-shell.json (only the plugins shipped
#     here; the drawer at 6 columns; Omarchy's idle values, kept off by its
#     stay-awake toggle; Omarchy's 18 bar-widget-only plugins in
#     disabledPlugins, since omamobile.bar shows none of them and the shell
#     would still compile each at every start) and profile/home.json is new
#     (tablet-home.json: a 6x8 home grid with the image's apps), seeded by
#     the image build;
#   - 0001-tablet-quick-settings-tiles.patch: no hotspot, torch, location,
#     NFC, fingerprint or rotation-lock tiles (0005 puts mobile data back, 0006
#     the rotation lock, 0013 location);
#   - 0002-wifi-wpa2-without-sae.patch: the BCM4358 firmware has no SAE
#     (WPA3), so the Wi-Fi panel joins a WPA3/WPA2 SSID with a WPA2-PSK
#     profile through nmcli instead of Quickshell's key-mgmt=sae one (needs
#     iw, to ask the radio);
#   - 0003-tablet-drawer-opens-light.patch: the app drawer opens without
#     rescanning every icon directory and without unfolding the keyboard
#     (half the CPU and a third less GPU per opening);
#   - 0004-tablet-quiet-pollers.patch: the home toggles watch the
#     notification service's settings file instead of a `qs ipc` call every
#     30 s, and the bar starts its modem and call watchers only when the
#     bar's cellWatch / callWatch setting is true (true in tablet-shell.json);
#   - 0005-tablet-modem.patch: the mobile data tile, through NetworkManager's
#     gsm connection instead of the Pixel's omamobile-sit.
#   - 0006-tablet-rotation.patch: the Rotation tile back, over t715-rotate
#     (docs/image/ROTATION.md), and a Rotate tile for a turn by hand.
#   - 0007-tablet-mobile-settings.patch: the mobile data tile opens Réseau
#     mobile (t715-mobile-settings) on a long press, or a tap with no connection.
#   - 0008-tablet-tiles-that-work.patch: Airplane mode turns the modem off too,
#     the Hotspot tile is back and shows its password, no Speaker on the call card.
#   - 0009-upstream-bottom-strip-keyboard-on-pill.patch and
#     0010-upstream-app-names-in-recents.patch: from upstream's 0.2.40 to 0.2.43.
#   - 0011-tablet-set-pin.patch: omamobile-set-pin says tablet, and sudo asks once
#     a password is chosen.
#   - 0012-tablet-back-gesture.patch: the edge swipe does what the Back key does.
# Dropped (phone-only, or replaced by the image's touch layer P1):
#   - plugins omamobile.fingerprint, .update (needs omamobile-update),
#     .access (camera and location permission sheet);
#   - bin/omamobile-fp-enroll, -nfc-open (and its
#     unit), -keys (t715-keys has the keys), -sleepd (and its unit; suspend
#     is masked on this tablet), -onboarding (the owner sets a PIN from the
#     menu), -portal-access (and portal/), -open-intent (Android links);
#   - hypr/phone.lua (rootfs/t715-tablet.lua replaces it), the OSK pieces P1
#     already has (environment.d/20-omamobile-osk.conf, the fcitx5 drop-in,
#     squeekboard's terminal layout) and omamobile-osk-guard (and its unit):
#     one mechanism per function, see docs/image/ROOTFS.md;
#   - xdg-desktop-portal-gnome's file chooser drop-in and portals.conf, the
#     "AI Agent" desktop entry (no agent runs on armv7h);
#   - depends on omamobile-apps (needs neard, not in ALARM armv7h),
#     omamobile-owl-widgets (the OWL built-ins: optional and heavy, off),
#     xdg-desktop-portal-gnome, foot/xdg-terminal-exec and iproute2.
#
# Source: the GitHub tarball of derekross/omarchy-mobile at 5f7ba48 (MIT;
# squeekboard's layout, not shipped here, is GPL-3.0-or-later), checked by
# sha256; only packages/omamobile-shell is extracted.
# Build: tools/build-pkg omamobile-shell. Image: rootfs/install-mobile.sh,
# rootfs/omarchy-user-setup.sh; checks: tests/verify-rootfs.sh.

# Maintainer (upstream): Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>

pkgname=omamobile-shell
pkgver=0.2.32
pkgrel=1.15
pkgdesc="Omarchy Mobile's touch shell for Omarchy's shell: status bar, quick settings, launcher, recents, home, back swipe (SM-T715 tablet build)"
arch=(any)
url="https://github.com/derekross/omarchy-mobile"
license=(MIT)
depends=(omarchy 'omamobile-omarchy>=0.1.11' bash python python-dbus python-gobject
         qt6-declarative squeekboard jq inotify-tools bluez bluez-utils
         networkmanager iw brightnessctl curl pipewire wireplumber 'omatel-agent>=0.2.1')
optdepends=('wf-recorder: the Screen record tile'
            'khal: the home screen calendar'
            'playerctl: media keys for the home screen media widget')
checkdepends=(python)
install=omamobile-shell.install
_commit=5f7ba487cec6ca66ee04606be9d71d1aad855ea0
_tarball=omarchy-mobile-${_commit:0:7}.tar.gz
_dir=omarchy-mobile-$_commit/packages/omamobile-shell
source=("$_tarball::https://github.com/derekross/omarchy-mobile/archive/$_commit.tar.gz"
        0001-tablet-quick-settings-tiles.patch
        0002-wifi-wpa2-without-sae.patch
        0003-tablet-drawer-opens-light.patch
        0004-tablet-quiet-pollers.patch
